.TH WC 1
.SH NAME
wc \- word count
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wc
[
.B \-lwc
]
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wc
counts lines, words and bytes in the named
.IR files ,
or in the standard input if no file is named.
A word is a maximal string of characters
delimited by spaces, tabs, newlines or carriage returns.
.PP
If the optional argument is present,
just the specified counts (lines, words or bytes)
are selected by the letters
.BR l ,
.BR w ,
or
.BR c .
Otherwise all three
.RB ( \-lwc )
are reported.
Each count is right-justified in a field of 7 characters,
followed by the file's name when one was given.
When more than one file is named, a line marked
.B total
follows.
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/wc/main.odin
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B "can't open"
when a file could not be opened.
The other files are still counted.
.SH BUGS
.I Wc
counts bytes, not runes.
There is no
.B \-r
and no
.BR \-b .
